DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("e^((sin(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("sqrt((ln((10/(x)))))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("(-infinity, 10] - ((-infinity, infinity) - (((4, 14) U [4, 10]))) U ((4, 14))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("[4, 10] U [4, 10] U ((4, 14) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((-infinity, 10]))) U (4, 14)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-10, -4, -2} U ({-1, 1, 9} U {-10, -4, -2}) U {-3, 2}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({-1, 1, 9} U {-1, 1, 9}) U {-1, 1, 9} U {-3, 2} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -4, -2})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`4+6+12-3`]? [_____]{Formula('19')}
---

[`2+12-13+11/14`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('1.78571428571')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -4, -2\}`]
- [`B = \{-1, 1, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{-3, 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup (B \cup A) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B \cup B) \cup B \cup C \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 4 \leq x \leq 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 4 < x < 14\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \leq 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cap ((B \cup A)) \cup (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A \cup A \cup (B \cap (C)) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, 0, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 10, -4, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -3, -9, 1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-6, 0, 9>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, 0, 9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, -4, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, 0, 9>") . Compute("<10, -4, -8>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -9, 1>") x Compute("<-6, 0, 9>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -1, 0, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, -9, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -9, 6>") . Compute("<-1, 0, 7>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-3, -9, 6>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -9, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, 0, 7>") . Compute("<-3, -9, 6>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
